$( <MM> <PROOF_ASST> THEOREM=sqfdvdsum  LOC_AFTER=?

* The sum over the squarefree divisors of N of the product of the values of G over the prime factors is the product of 1 + ( G ` p ) over the prime factors of N.

s1::simpl |- ( ( N e. NN /\ G : Prime --> CC ) -> N e. NN )
s2::simpr |- ( ( N e. NN /\ G : Prime --> CC ) -> G : Prime --> CC )
s3::cbvrabv |- { p e. Prime | p || N } = { q e. Prime | q || N }
s4:s3:a1i |- ( ( N e. NN /\ G : Prime --> CC ) -> { p e. Prime | p || N } = { q e. Prime | q || N } )
